# Title: Renamed Visual Studio Code Tunnel Execution
# ID: 2cf29f11-e356-4f61-98c0-1bdb9393d6da
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2023-09-28
# Tags: attack.command-and-control, attack.t1071.001, attack.t1219
# Description: Detects renamed Visual Studio Code tunnel execution. Attackers can abuse this functionality to establish a C2 channel
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((((NOT _exists_:process.pe.original_file_name AND process.command_line:*.exe tunnel) OR ((process.command_line:*.exe tunnel* AND process.command_line:*--accept-server-license-terms*)) OR ((process.command_line:*tunnel * AND process.command_line:*service* AND process.command_line:*internal-run* AND process.command_line:*tunnel-service.log*))) AND NOT (((process.executable:*\\code-tunnel.exe OR process.executable:*\\code.exe)))) OR ((process.parent.command_line:* tunnel AND process.executable:*\\cmd.exe AND (process.command_line:*/d /c * AND process.command_line:*\\servers\\Stable-* AND process.command_line:*code-server.cmd*)) AND NOT (((process.parent.executable:*\\code-tunnel.exe OR process.parent.executable:*\\code.exe)))))
